       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In overdose it can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Here are some options:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf you tell me which dose you want, I'll enter it right away. If you meant to treat uncontrolled hypertension, adding a second agent from a different class is usually safer than going above 10 mg. That decision is for the prescriber."
