       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. It's five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. I can't verify claims about the patient or prior approvals, so confirmation alone doesn't let me go above that limit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose. I can also enter 5 mg, the usual starting dose.\n- **Suggest adding a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough to control the blood pressure, a drug from another class (an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic) is the standard next step. That decision is for the prescriber.\n- **Route it through pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there is an unusual clinical reason for this dose, they can review it and handle it outside my ordering workflow.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
